### Candidate A
- Strengths (reported by me) – anticipates dangerous situations; sees complex connections; excellent spatial vision; very good leadership qualities.
- Weaknesses (reported by me) – unorganized; resistant to criticism.

### Candidate B
- Strengths (reported by agent 3) – very conscientious; handles stress well; good at assessing weather conditions; excellent computer skills.
- Weaknesses (reported by agent 3) – pretentious/pretentious demeanor; occasional wrong tone; can be grumpy; can be uncooperative.

### Candidate C
- Strengths (reported by agent 3) – makes correct decisions quickly; 100 % reliable; creates a positive atmosphere with crew.
- Weaknesses (reported by agent 3) – difficulty communicating ideas; egocentric; not very willing to further his education.

### Candidate D
- Strengths (reported by agent 2) – takes responsibility seriously; solves problems extremely well; high concentration; responds adequately to unexpected events.
- Weaknesses (reported by agent 2) – regarded as arrogant; relatively weak leadership; hot temper; “know‑it‑all” reputation.

## Other Agents' Positions
- agent_2 – votes Candidate D; emphasizes responsibility, problem‑solving, concentration, calm response to unexpected events; notes hot temper and know‑it‑all as crew‑cooperation risks.
- agent_3 – votes Candidate B; emphasizes conscientiousness, stress handling, reliability; notes pretentious demeanor and tone issues.

## Open Issues Blocking Consensus
1. Crew‑interaction impact – severity of interpersonal drawbacks for A (unorganized, criticism‑resistant), B (pretentious, grumpy/uncooperative), and D (arrogance, hot temper, know‑it‑all) on long‑duration flight safety and crew cohesion.
2. Leadership vs. organization for A – does A’s strong leadership offset risks from poor organization and resistance to feedback?
3. Comparative severity of attitude issues – which candidate’s attitude problems pose the greatest safety‑relevant threat?
4. Candidate C’s trade‑offs – can perfect reliability and positive crew atmosphere compensate for communication difficulties and limited drive for further education?

